 Aztecs arrived in central Mexico, they were driven onto a swampy island in Lake Texcoco.", "s": 6.722, "e": 13.6}, {"text": "Instead of leaving, they engineered chinampas, floating rectangular gardens woven from reeds and anchored with willow trees.", "s": 13.72, "e": 22.41}, {"text": "Over two centuries, they connected these islands with massive stone causeways, aqueducts, and canals.", "s": 22.53, "e": 29.642}, {"text": "When Spanish conquistadors arrived in 1519, Tenochtitlan had over 200,000 residents, botanical gardens, and running water, leaving European soldiers wondering if they were dreaming.", "s": 29.762, "e": 44.476}]}